The only ssim2 regression below the -0.3 acceptance gate is 1025469
e8/e9 d=4 (-0.847 SSIM2, -0.98% bytes, +6.4% butteraugli).

W44-118 follow-on: qac-scale re-tune
------------------------------------

The W44-105/107/108/109 qac-scale chain was tuned against the LEGACY
optimistic buttloop measurement (which reported scores 2-47× lower
than reality). With the W44-117 fix, the buttloop sees the SAME EPF
as the decoder → measures accurately → converges on a slightly
different quant_field equilibrium.

On screenshot-class cells (terminal, codec_wiki) the new equilibrium
is BETTER (SSIM2 +0.4 to +0.9) because the qac-scale chain's 4×
seed scale lifts the buttloop into a region where the now-accurate
measurement still requires the same lift.

On photo cells the picture is mixed — 1025469 e8 d=4 regresses
0.85 SSIM2 because the buttloop's previously-optimistic score gave
the encoder permission to over-quantize one specific pattern; now
that the buttloop sees the real cost, it pulls back the quantization
slightly and the qac-scale chain's 4× seed scale becomes the binding
constraint.

W44-118 candidate work (NOT shipped in W44-117):
  (a) Decouple the W44-105 chain's `is_screenshot` from the W44-117
      seed compute — already done structurally; both gates fire
      independently. The interaction is via the converged quant_field.
  (b) Re-sweep the W44-105 `DEFAULT_BUTTLOOP_SCREENSHOT_QF_SEED_SCALE`
      (currently 4.0) against the new W44-117 buttloop accuracy.
      Lower scales (2-3) may now be sufficient on screenshot cells AND
      avoid the photo over-correction.
  (c) Lower the W44-109 `effort <= 7` scales (currently 2.0 at e5/e6,
      3.0 at e7) — these don't interact with the buttloop (W44-117
      fires only at e>=8 when buttloop runs) but they may now be
      sub-optimal vs a different content discriminator.
  (d) Remove the qac-scale chain entirely — high-risk, would need a
      wide bench to verify no terminal regression.

Acceptance gate evaluation
--------------------------

| Gate | Target | Result |
|---|---|---|
| EPF sharpness seed computed once before buttloop, used in apply_epf | wired | PASS |
| Per-step dump residual drops ≤0.03 R on 1025469 d=2 e8 | yes | PARTIAL (0.054 max-abs; mean 0.000174 -69%) |
| Paired interleaved A/B on 30+ cells: no SSIM2 regression > 0.3 vs W44-109 baseline | 0 | FAIL (2 cells, both 1025469 e8/e9 d=4 at -0.85) |
| Hash-lock regen sub-100-cell + sub-200-byte | <100 | PASS (0 hash-locks changed) |
| cargo test --lib passes | passes | PASS (1279 passed) |
| Multi-decoder roundtrip djxl + jxl-rs on 3 cells | 3 PASS | PASS (3/3, both decoders) |
| buttloop wall ≤ +20% vs W44-109 baseline at e8 | TBD | NOT MEASURED (paired bench timed encode but didn't isolate buttloop wall) |

Per task spec decision tree:
  "EPF residual drops but qac-scale chain causes regressions: ship EPF
   fix + document qac-scale re-tune as W44-118."

→ SHIP W44-117 + file W44-118 follow-on.

Hash-lock impact
----------------

The synthetic 32×32 / 48×48 fixtures used by `tests/hash_lock_features.rs`
go through the encoder path with mask1x1=None (pixel_domain_loss is
off by default at the effort levels they use, OR ac_strategy_enabled
is false). The W44-117 gate falls back to uniform-4 → 36/36
hash-locks BYTE-IDENTICAL.

Files modified
--------------

* `jxl-encoder/src/vardct/butteraugli_loop.rs` (+~80 lines):
  new mask1x1 param + seed compute block + env override JXL_W44_117_DISABLE
* `jxl-encoder/src/vardct/encoder.rs` (+~8 lines):
  plumb mask1x1.as_deref() into the buttloop call
* `jxl-encoder/src/vardct/bitstream.rs` (+~5 lines):
  pass None (animation frames don't precompute mask1x1)
* `jxl-encoder/examples/w44_117_paired_ab.rs` (NEW, ~300 lines)
* `jxl-encoder/examples/w44_117_decoder_check.rs` (NEW, ~80 lines)
* `jxl-encoder/Cargo.toml` (+12 lines): register the new examples
* `docs/LIBJXL_DIVERGENCES.md`: Section D row updated, Section F row
  updated to reference W44-117 + W44-118
* `benchmarks/w44_117_paired_ab_2026-05-20.{tsv,meta}` (NEW)

DO NOT
------

* DO NOT remove the W44-105/107/108/109 qac-scale chain in this chunk
  — that's W44-118 (separate chunk, separate bench).
* DO NOT remove the per-iter compute_epf_sharpness call inside the
  buttloop's `for iter in 0..iters+1` loop — there is no such call;
  the seed is computed ONCE before the loop. Option A (per-iter
  recompute) was rejected per the W44-116 fix-shape ranking
  (~10-30% buttloop slowdown vs Option B's one-shot cost).
* DO NOT respawn FMA precision claims (per the binding directive).
  The R/G residual is the sharpness map mismatch, not FMA.
